var e=`## Fabric Mods

List of mods developed using Fabric Loader and Fabric API, big mod loader to help to create Minecraft mods.

### Biome Loot Table

Dev test for Eufonia Studio a while ago.

Changes how the loot tables are being handle by the game. Adding server side configs for modifying loot depending on which biome the player at that moment, also giving the possibility to select the loot table based on a config list.

Check more on: [[biome_loot_table|Biome Loot Table]]

### Cobblemon Legendary Spawn

Add news config to modify how-when a custom list of Pokémons (Normally legendaries) will spawn, this handles things like flying/water spawn, special biome/weather conditions and probably things, all inside a simple and fast config.

Check more on: [[cobblemon_legendary_spawn|Cobblemon Legendary Spawn]]

### Cobblemon Raids

Invite and create a party of 3 players to start a raid!! Only 3 lives for team, each loss cost a live, and you need to fight through 3 Pokémon and then fight the boss (Normally a legendary/special Pokémon) with special abilities, after defeated you have the change to capture it. GUIs, config and everything was used here!!.

Check more on: [[cobblemon_raids|Cobblemon Raids]]

### Exploration Revamped

Adds several QoL features related to exploration and movement around your world. Trying to change a lot of mechanics and day to day features of the original game, specially focused on adding new items, crafting recipes and overriding default mechanics.

Check more on: [[exploration_revamped|Exploration Revamped]]


### Herobrines Like

Some weird things are happening in the world, you must convert the normal ores into a new variant, craft a new weapon and armor, explore for unusual variations in your world and try to fight against this dangerous creature called Herobrine.

Check more on: [[herobrines_like|Herobrines Like]]

### Hour Limit

Mod that limits the max playtime of all the players based on a specific value. Giving a lineal mechanic where each player enters after the last one, saving their progress and items. All this to make a video that is: 50 players have 1 hour of playtime each one, and they should finish the game.

Check more on: [[hour_limit|Hour Limit]]

### Kit Custom Enchants

Custom and powerful enchants to minecraft, removes all the vanilla enchantments and provides very visual effects.

Check more on: [[kit_custom_enchants|Kit Custom Enchants]]

### Mobility Changer

Change all the piston rules with a new item called Mobility Changer, now you could move block entities like chest or beacons.

Check more on: [[mobility_changer|Mobility Changer]]

### Multihitboxlib (Fabric Port)

Multihitbox lib is a library for handling advanced multihitbox mobs, Syncing hitboxes with geckolib bones too (and with Azurelib). This is made for handling easy multipart entities and making complex geckolib animations easily.

In this case I was asked to make the Fabric port of the 1.20.1 version.

Check more on: [[multihitbox_lib|MultihitboxLib]]

### Odyssey Pokedrop

Adds a new custom system to add drops to the Pokemons, with a Pokémon whitelist and supporting item nbts and multiple World loader. Mod made to work with Fabric-Spigot plugins.

Check more on: [[odyssey_pokedrop|Odyssey Pokedrop]]

### Sad Ditto

This mod's purpose is to prevent the "Bottle Cap" items from the \`cobblemon utility\` mod from being used on Ditto. Made to avoid broken Dittos inside the server due to this mod.

Commission made for Dystopia Network (Minecraft server)

Check more on: [[sad_ditto|Sad Ditto]]

### Shiny Converter

Add a new GUI to change your shinies into custom items (NBT data support), config for changing GUI placement, text format and different Pokémon checks.

This mod was made for Fabric and Forge for Minecraft 1.20.1.

Check more on: [[shiny_converter|Shiny Converter]]

### Illegal Mobs (April Fools Collection)

Recreating a list of mobs that were included in all Minecraft's April Fools snapshots with their original features, renders and behaviors.

Check more on: [[illegal_mobs|Illegal Mobs]]`;export{e as default};